WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.987
Let’s walk through Manage session operations.

00:00:02.987 --> 00:00:06.725
Keep the selected session stable while moving between settings tabs

00:00:06.725 --> 00:00:06.900
.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:10.150
Sessions, participants, decks, plugins, and exports

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:13.412
are related operational surfaces, but each has a different

00:00:13.412 --> 00:00:15.213
owner and consequence.

00:00:15.213 --> 00:00:18.500
On this slide, the Simulation Settings tabs also cover

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:22.750
live sessions, participant rosters, facilitator deck assignments

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.137
, plugins, and export controls.

00:00:25.685 --> 00:00:28.410
In practice, use the correct tab for the operational

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:32.435
task and preserve the current session selection before changing participants

00:00:32.435 --> 00:00:34.873
, decks, plugins, or exports.

00:00:34.873 --> 00:00:37.710
Before you continue, verify these points:

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:40.047
Sessions establish the active run.

00:00:40.047 --> 00:00:42.910
Participants and decks determine who can act and what is

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:43.998
projected.

00:00:43.998 --> 00:00:47.035
Plugins and exports remain session-scoped.

00:00:47.035 --> 00:00:50.385
Use the highlighted Settings tabs area as your visual reference

00:00:50.385 --> 00:00:52.060
while you complete this check.
